<bioghist id="ref175">
<head>Biography/History</head>
<p>Donald Carl Eugster is a composer, lyriciststs, and arranger for musicals and the theater. Eugster was born in Hollywood, California on April 14, 1925. Eugster played piano and French horn in the United States Navy band while he served from 1943-1946. Eugster scored his first musical, Alice in Wonderland, during his undergraduate education at UCLA. Eugster currently lives in Los Angeles and continues to compose and perform across a variety of genres.</p>
</bioghist>
<scopecontent id="ref176">
<head>Scope and Content</head>
<p>The collection contains compositions from his career including music from Alice in Wonderland, A Christmas Carol, and Hurly Burly. This collection also contains photos, correspondence, and recordings from Eugster’s professional life.</p>
</scopecontent>
